canvas 1
collection @gatekeeper-build-plan "Gatekeeper build — removals, done, tasks" {

  node @rm-table concept "Removed capabilities — third version, corrected against two audits" role=warning size=large {
    table @rm-t columns=["Removed", "Affects", "What it does today", "Plain words — what changes for you", "Risk to weigh"] {
      row @rm-r1 cells=["G0 · Edit lock (three places: workspace-session.ts:1064-1072, canvas/core/interaction/changes.ts:22, submission-session.ts:60)", "Your screen (all diagrams)", "While an earlier edit, undo or review is still being processed, the app refuses any new edit. The lock exists in three separate places, not one.", "If you click or drag twice quickly, the second edit is currently dropped. After the change, both edits go to the server. The one-edit-in-flight guard stays, but its answer is 'wait', never a legality verdict.", "Without the lock, the second edit arrives on a stale base and the server answers revision-conflict. Turn-taking and rebase rules (stage 2) must exist FIRST, or fast editing gets worse, not better."]
      row @rm-r2 cells=["G1 · Movement review (the modules-only review interrupt)", "Your screen (module diagrams only)", "When you drag a node in a module diagram, the app can interrupt with a review offering two kinds of options: rearrange the section, or expand the group.", "The review interrupt dies, and with it the rearrange shortcut. The EXPAND half survives as the 'keep in' answer — but only on module diagrams, where it works today. Keep-in on plain groups (flow, tree, er, sequence) is new work, budgeted in stage 5.", "The rearrange shortcut has no replacement in this plan — confirm you do not rely on it. The review teardown is the biggest deletion in the build (~1,600 lines)."]
      row @rm-r3 cells=["G2 · Planner hard-fail ('captured group missing')", "Your screen (mostly module diagrams)", "Groups and trees can be collapsed so their children are hidden (folding). A drag touching collapsed or absent content can stop with the error 'captured group missing'; the server is never asked, so nothing is saved. On the placement path this is already caught as stale-target.", "A drag that fails with that error today will instead reach the server and either work or get a clear refusal.", "More cases now reach the server. Until the server has answers for them, you may see refusals where you previously saw a failed drag with a technical message — so the refusals must be readable (stage 9)."]
      row @rm-r4 cells=["G3 · Browser roads engine (route-preview.ts)", "Your screen (module diagrams)", "Module diagrams draw wires between modules along planned routes (roads). Today your browser re-computes these routes itself before the server is asked. Keep-in's expand also borrows this local solve for its preview.", "Roads still draw exactly as today, and the visibility toggle still works — only who computes them changes. Your browser stops calculating and asks the server's existing preview instead; keep-in's preview switches to the server too. If the server cannot be reached, you see 'judge unreachable' (a proposed message).", "Previews are full server renders, so they may appear later than today's local solve — this is unmeasured, and a drop that previews then commits pays two renders. Measure before stage 6."]
      row @rm-r5 cells=["G4 · Journal wedge — MOSTLY FIXED ALREADY (submission-session.ts)", "Your screen", "The app records each edit it sends. A plainly refused edit already frees the next edit, and recovery buttons already exist (PR #104, RequestRecovery.tsx). The remaining gap: an edit whose receipt was never found (state 'retryable') blocks new edits and cannot be dismissed.", "An unlucky edit can be abandoned explicitly, and then you keep working. Today that wedge has no way out.", "Abandoning must be sure the edit never landed — the existing reconcile/retry check first, so nothing is applied twice."]
      row @rm-r6 cells=["The browser as a decider (all five above)", "Your screen", "Five checks inside your browser decide what is allowed before the server is asked. For a human edit, the browser's answer is final today — the server may never see the edit.", "Your browser presents and the server decides. Humans and agents are answered by the same place — and that place largely exists today (admission, planner, feasibility render, atomic commit, plus a preview route humans can already use).", "Every answer now needs a server round-trip, and refusals come from the server. The design accepts this; it is the point of the change."]
    }
    text @rm-note "Corrected against two Opus 5.5 audits: G0 lives in three places, G1's expand half survives (modules-only), keep-in on plain groups is new work, and G4's real gap is the undismissable retryable edit. If a row is unclear or unacceptable, raise it before the build starts." role=caption
  }

  node @done-table concept "Definition of done — exact checks, exact pass conditions" role=primary size=large {
    table @done-t columns=["#", "The exact check", "Execute — command / function", "Pass condition (math)"] {
      row @done-r1 cells=["D1", "On every diagram mode where a node can leave a group, drag node N out of group G: the drop lands, a popup offers keep-in / move-out / cancel, and choosing move-out commits and survives a reload", "Headless browser per mode; popup = drop-choice.askMeaning() (proposed); keep-in = movement-expand.buildExpandOption() (modules) + new plain-group keep-in; move-out = regroupSections()", "(popup options = {keep-in, move-out, cancel}; after reload parent(N) != G; modes: flow, tree, er, modules confirmed in stage 3; sequence group-drag verified in stage 3 or D1 scopes it out in writing)"]
      row @done-r2 cells=["D2", "Send the same SEMANTIC edit at the same base revision R once as a browser drag and once as DSL text (an equivalent edit — the identical request is impossible: actor must match the caller and agents cannot use the model planner)", "Browser drag -> admit -> prepare(preview=true); CLI: pnpm canvas preview FILE --revision R; if committing, pnpm canvas apply REQUEST_ID", "(verdict_browser(R) = verdict_CLI(R); if both commit, new_revision_browser = new_revision_CLI)"]
      row @done-r3 cells=["D3", "No browser code decides LEGALITY before the server is asked. Transport guards may remain (one edit in flight, stale-gesture) but their answer is 'wait / retry', never a legality verdict", "grep for legality refusals on the apps/web drag path; live drag with the server stopped", "(legality verdicts issued in apps/web = 0; stopped server -> message = 'judge unreachable' (proposed message) and local verdicts = 0)"]
      row @done-r4 cells=["D4", "An edit whose receipt was never found (state 'retryable') can be dismissed, and the next edit then commits", "Force a retryable entry; abandon it via the extended RequestRecovery; then commit a valid edit E2", "(journal(E1).state = abandoned; outcome(E2) = committed; no edit applied twice)"]
      row @done-r5 cells=["D5", "Every refusal is plain words plus options; no raw codes on any user-visible surface", "Trigger each refusal type (rule broken, not drawable, revision conflict, judge unreachable) -> diagnostics.toHumanWords() (proposed; extends the PR #104 mapping)", "(raw codes shown = 0; options shown = {retry, adjust, cancel} for every refusal type)"]
      row @done-r6 cells=["D6", "Module diagrams have no modules-only review interrupt and no browser roads engine; one law set serves all modes", "grep for modules-only branches on the drag path; run D1 on a modules diagram", "(modules-only drag-path branches = 0; D1(modules) = pass)"]
      row @done-r7 cells=["D7", "pnpm check shows no new failures versus main", "Run pnpm check on the branch; diff the failures against the recorded main baseline", "(new failures on branch = 0)"]
      row @done-r8 cells=["D8", "The known broken module-node drag on main (PR #106's target) is fixed or explicitly deferred in writing", "Headless drag of a module node, or append the written decision to this collection", "(node position after commit = drop position) or (written deferral exists in this collection)"]
    }
    text @done-note "These are gates, unlike the line estimates. If a row cannot be proven, the build is not done. D2 and D4 were rewritten after the audits: D2 was impossible as first written; D4 first described a problem PR #104 already fixed, then a reconcile that already exists — the real gap is the undismissable retryable edit." role=caption
  }

  node @task-table concept "Task list — the stage tracker (read top to bottom = build order)" role=primary size=large {
    table @task-t columns=["Stage", "Task", "What the builder is doing", "Task done when…", "Est. lines (+/-)", "What you will observe", "Achieves"] {
      row @task-r1 cells=["1 of 10", "Abandon the undismissable edit", "submission-session.ts + records/submission.ts + submissions.ts + RequestRecovery.tsx: a retryable edit (no receipt found) can be abandoned; reconcile/retry already exist and are reused", "A retryable entry is abandoned, then a valid edit commits (D4)", "+55 / -10", "A diagram stuck after an unlucky save can be unstuck explicitly, without losing work.", "D4"]
      row @task-r2 cells=["2 of 10", "Turn-taking: rebase rules", "diagram-planners.ts + authoring-store.ts + admission.ts: a revision-conflict answer says what changed and how to rebase — in the files where conflicts actually originate", "A second quick edit gets a rebase answer, not a dead end", "+50 / -15", "Nothing yet. This exists so stage 8 does not make fast editing worse.", "enables D3"]
      row @task-r3 cells=["3 of 10", "The group-edge popup", "drop-choice.ts (new, drafts) + drafts/regroup.ts + CanvasSurface.tsx: the drop lands, then keep-in / move-out / cancel at the drop spot; verify group drags on sequence diagrams", "The popup works on every diagram mode (D1 scope settled in writing)", "+210 / -10", "Drop a node on a group's edge and a popup asks: keep in group, move out, or cancel.", "D1"]
      row @task-r4 cells=["4 of 10", "Capture and plan both meanings", "movement-capture.ts stops throwing; plan.ts + regroup.ts turn one ambiguous drop into two candidate requests (keep-in, move-out)", "A group-edge drop yields both plans; nothing throws", "+175 / -75", "Drags that used to stop with 'captured group missing' now work or get a clear refusal.", "D1, D3"]
      row @task-r5 cells=["5 of 10", "Keep-in: expand rewired + plain groups", "movement-expand.ts: its preview switches from the in-browser solve to the server preview (the solve it borrows today dies in stage 6). Plain-group keep-in (flow, tree, er, sequence) is built new — no mode has group-grow today", "keep-in works on modules via expand and on one plain-group mode via the new path; both persist after reload", "+140 / -40", "'keep in' grows the group around the node. Modules reuses existing code; plain groups are new.", "D1"]
      row @task-r6 cells=["6 of 10", "Route-preview asks the server", "route-preview.ts: the in-browser roads solve is deleted; previews call the existing server preview route. Measure the two-renders-per-drop cost first", "No roads engine in the browser; browser and CLI share one pipeline (D2)", "+30 / -70", "Wire previews on module diagrams may appear later; they match what the server will commit.", "D2, D3, D6"]
      row @task-r7 cells=["7 of 10", "Movement-review teardown", "movement.ts, movement-rearrange.ts, movement-preview.ts, movement-intent.ts, MovementReview.tsx, records/movement.ts, compose.ts, tests/movement.test.ts: the review machinery is gutted. Ships together with stage 8 — the call sites live in workspace-session.ts (counted there)", "The review interrupt is gone from every drag path; the build compiles with workspace-session edited", "+105 / -1616", "Module drags stop being interrupted by the review. The rearrange shortcut is gone (removals, row G1).", "D3, D6"]
      row @task-r8 cells=["8 of 10", "Edit locks removed", "workspace-session.ts + interaction/changes.ts: the lock is deleted in two places; the submission lock stays as a transport guard whose answer is 'wait' (allowed by D3)", "No local legality verdict on the drag path (D3); rapid edits get server answers in turn", "+45 / -510", "Rapid successive edits stop being silently dropped. Requires stage 2 first.", "D3"]
      row @task-r9 cells=["9 of 10", "Refusals in human words", "diagnostics.ts + authoring api.ts + feasibility.ts: the laws' typed reasons surface and the existing plain-English mapping (PR #104) renders them", "Every refusal surface passes D5", "+85 / 0", "A refused edit tells you why in plain words and offers retry, adjust, or cancel.", "D5"]
      row @task-r10 cells=["10 of 10", "Modules loses special cases + session split", "Delete the remaining modules-only branches; decide and land (or write down the deferral of) the workspace-session split", "D6 passes; the split lands or its deferral is written down", "included above", "Module diagrams behave like every other diagram. No module-only popups.", "D6"]
    }
    text @task-note "During the build, 'stage 4 of 10' refers to this table. Line estimates sum exactly to B.4's third-count totals (+895 / -2346); stage 10 is the removal half of earlier stages plus a decision, not new work. D7 and D8 are whole-build checks made after stage 10, so no single stage owns them." role=caption
  }

  section @s-removed "1 · Removed capabilities — what changes, and the risk of each (corrected)" mode=flow direction=right order=0 {
    show @rm-table
  }

  section @s-done "2 · Definition of done — exact checks, exact pass conditions" mode=flow direction=right order=1 {
    show @done-table
  }

  section @s-tasks "3 · Task list — ten stages, tracked here" mode=flow direction=right order=2 {
    show @task-table
  }
}
